}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}^{′} & =f(x,y) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & =f\\left({{field-1}},\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx\\right) \\\\ {y}_{2}^{′} & =f\\left(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,{{field-2}}\\right) \\\\ {y}_{3}^{′} & =f(x+Δx,\\,{{field-3}})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe increment in $y$ using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method with step size $Δx$ is computed as the weighted average of four sample slopes:\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{1}^{′}=f({x}_{1},{y}_{1})$ is the estimated slope at $$\n\\displaystyle ({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=\\left(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx\\right),\n$$\n\n- ${y}_{2}^{′}=f({x}_{2},{y}_{2})$ is the estimated slope at $$\n\\displaystyle ({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=\\left(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx\\right),\n$$\n\n- ${y}_{3}^{′}=f({x}_{3},{y}_{3})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{3},{y}_{3})=(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390907 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e6eed83-83ce-545e-bdb5-d5c028a8d37d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390909} {:answer/id #uuid "0569c095-e03a-53ae-8b2c-2a081af44aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390910} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c54676-3491-5208-a1db-82bc598123c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390911} {:answer/id #uuid "4d852899-6223-5333-a301-6f9971200048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390912} {:answer/id #uuid "daef89c6-3cb1-55f9-8684-52f37c7bc5be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390913}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390909} :answer-field/id #uuid "2420d840-3b85-5ad8-9b12-4c80cfd6bb59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "927bdcac-2749-5a1c-8331-70b709fa149b" :question/math-academy-id "q-33132" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩$ at the point where $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-{e}^{-t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨-{e}^{-(0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+{e}^{-(0)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,-{e}^{-(0)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-{e}^{-(0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0),\\,-{e}^{-(0)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-0+1,\\,-1-0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(0)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6eed83-83ce-545e-bdb5-d5c028a8d37d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390909} {:answer/id #uuid "0569c095-e03a-53ae-8b2c-2a081af44aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390910} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c54676-3491-5208-a1db-82bc598123c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390911} {:answer/id #uuid "4d852899-6223-5333-a301-6f9971200048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390912} {:answer/id #uuid "daef89c6-3cb1-55f9-8684-52f37c7bc5be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390913} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391568 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bd0b65e-3a0f-5994-9689-9aef5b5c9454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6{e}^{-x}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391570} {:answer/id #uuid "3fae5784-6514-5371-820c-1909539d4c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391571} {:answer/id #uuid "58c34fda-7cad-508d-a7f2-d8bf06c08b7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391572} {:answer/id #uuid "7448e8d2-a22f-59f6-bc6b-c65f6e7cf2de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391573}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391573} :answer-field/id #uuid "d308949f-707a-5a2c-802c-a0a17c33433a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4e6cf3c-fccb-5029-b604-d1593b0daddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391575} {:answer/id #uuid "1e61f74a-48e8-542c-a33f-c9fe7a376f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391576} {:answer/id #uuid "74653977-5fc1-57a5-a3e9-24eb70eb33c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391577} {:answer/id #uuid "fb69fbee-2b0a-5d6f-b11d-267cf756dd9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391578}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391577} :answer-field/id #uuid "2021aa17-0151-5e2d-987a-a1856edc5e53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6530e5db-b521-5f5c-99f7-59872d852e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-335402" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=6{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is already in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=6{e}^{2x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y\\right) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot 6{e}^{2x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =6{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =6{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =-6{e}^{-x}+C \\\\ y & =-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb9195b-384d-5b2f-bad0-6dd43e0f4b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391595} {:answer/id #uuid "f34ac63a-04a2-52a7-a90f-f8f4d8d09299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391596} {:answer/id #uuid "2d29d24c-fd03-58f5-91b9-3629bcaeee91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391597} {:answer/id #uuid "f585add5-def6-5238-932b-3a30184083f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391598} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f4e1e7-75e7-58c7-87b8-4747684ab781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391599}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391599} :answer-field/id #uuid "7806b0bb-9404-54a9-9afe-9fe5aae500c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d49da7f-4559-53d4-88e7-a4a538e83bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391601} {:answer/id #uuid "185130ca-9e63-5f95-8858-fbe1360a02af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391602} {:answer/id #uuid "24752170-0362-5a79-8550-d496d2deb223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391603} {:answer/id #uuid "7644849e-bdfd-532f-b35d-2dd327bd7b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391604}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391601} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a5f76ae-1afb-592e-a102-26dd10e20b42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3c6ef87c-1a0b-5973-8a1d-74f719874948" :question/math-academy-id "q-335806" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=2x{e}^{-x},\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=2x{e}^{-x}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y\\right) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 2x{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}y & =2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x}) & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{x} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ y & =({x}^{2}+C){e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =({0}^{2}+C){e}^{-0} \\\\ -2 & =(0+C)\\cdot 1 \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c71556-c8bb-509e-b7b6-813b830221cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391607} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc0fd51-b3d5-5b60-822b-55ce1a39a048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-2{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391608} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5f9c6d-a3bd-55c8-a595-021440af2d20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4-5{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391609} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff86545-6fe9-59ce-a43b-d596ae985d85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391610} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e86c18-962f-5498-8cd8-fd15eaf09b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391607} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c53fba-addc-5347-89bc-46926b4cec8a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68eff5b7-73e9-589d-b262-8718bbf64cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391613} {:answer/id #uuid "708406f2-8554-5163-8a8c-780da5f0a24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391614} {:answer/id #uuid "38c2efa8-509c-59df-90e0-5ff1a247796d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391615} {:answer/id #uuid "878ffcb1-ce95-5b25-bcf5-982716631d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391616}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391615} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0dfecd2-1e22-5e5a-aff3-e35469e93c9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cba95378-fbb4-59fe-bb7c-3f501d3e7ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335829" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=8,\\,y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4$ and $Q(x)=8.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{4x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4x}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y\\right) & ={e}^{4x}\\cdot 8 \\\\ {e}^{4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{4x}\\cdot y & =8{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x}) & =8{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 8{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =8\\left(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}\\right)+C \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =2{e}^{4x}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-4(0)} \\\\ -1 & =2+C(1) \\\\ C & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-3{e}^{-4x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e513d59-ec4b-56e0-a149-748a6164fa0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391633} {:answer/id #uuid "5b08fcdf-1c61-56cb-b330-8a9759c8a89e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391634} {:answer/id #uuid "8210e913-8fc4-50f7-87cd-8fd56787dfec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391635} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b489bc-4e90-59af-8076-7c8a1e2ef20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391636} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c3feb9-80f0-5263-bb9b-e4994b84169c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391637}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391633} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ffd0d69-a63d-58b1-a22c-7c7b302f6577" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "214d5c25-f05c-5b96-87cf-f66e123da8aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-33706" :question/problem "![](images/10/10ee30ddf508bf985e1c3a41491818723b57301412a5514e4a39c3bc13518acd.png)\n\nWhich integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g}(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}t,2-t\\operatorname{cos}t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=\\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)$ and $‖{\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t) & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}t),\\hspace{0.167em}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t\\operatorname{cos}t)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}t+t\\operatorname{cos}t,\\hspace{0.167em}t\\operatorname{sin}t-\\operatorname{cos}t⟩ \\\\ ‖{\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}t+t\\operatorname{cos}t)^{2}+(t\\operatorname{sin}t-\\operatorname{cos}t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t+2t\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t+{t}^{2}{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t+{t}^{2}{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t-2t\\operatorname{sin}t\\operatorname{cos}t+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L &={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }‖{\\mathbf{g}}^{'}(t)‖\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391654 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "405a5785-5b34-57dd-8ee6-7cf3c14c3b4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391656} {:answer/id #uuid "02c9e893-9d91-5235-b549-382b71a5543f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391657} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc97e04-8bc1-5d35-bd81-38e3fca740d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391658} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9976bc-fa6f-5d35-a147-d160f45c0036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391658} :answer-field/id #uuid "20192922-8171-54fa-90a2-ddc855fb0da5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a7efa86-b472-5ed5-b224-1426be141770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391661} {:answer/id #uuid "28cb4cfd-dc4e-58e9-9682-e66719264ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391662} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2aa6bc-5f1f-5b98-a317-03dc20826446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391663} {:answer/id #uuid "bdcc8170-82d1-59e4-8e50-50028abda132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391664}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391664} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb50e09f-3243-5b20-805e-de37af2e1718" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f5b12f52-bca9-597a-88b5-c5036d3e9da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-338027" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\n(3x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+\\left(xy+\\frac{3}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}\\left(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\right)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=3x+{y}^{2},\\,Q(x,y)=xy+\\frac{3}{x}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(x)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\n$\\,$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant." :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}\\left(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\right)=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}\\left(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\right)=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{1}{x}$ is a function of $x$ only, we can conclude that the integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int {x}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our equation by the integrating factor, we arrive at the following exact differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\left[(3x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+\\left(xy+\\frac{3}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}y\\right] & =0 \\\\ \\underbrace{(3{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2})}_{\\overset{~}{P}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\underbrace{({x}^{2}y+3)}_{\\overset{~}{Q}}\\,\\text{d}y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor this exact equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2},\\,\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)={x}^{2}y+3.\n$$\n\nTo solve the equation, let's first integrate $\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $y,$ which we'll call $F(y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{P}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+F(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's integrate $\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $x,$ which we'll call $G(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{2}y+3)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y+G(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we must have\n\n$$\nF(y)=3y,\\,G(x)={x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y=c.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d5e5efa-0ad9-5cb1-8007-def75d4c0f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391733} {:answer/id #uuid "181ce215-60ee-5a98-8d16-1f87a5c66bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391734} {:answer/id #uuid "c201762a-3b3f-52e3-a4c2-6f449ab4bd0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391735} {:answer/id #uuid "45bdee38-54f6-5e18-9b5f-1f916081c4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391736}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391736} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52979ca-88b2-53be-b424-0a20f99bf0c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391732} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02bcb740-d3b0-5e03-ac52-deeb78de3ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391738} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0496f9-803e-5f66-af97-d84ac1ef5ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391739} {:answer/id #uuid "917a7312-27b6-560b-80be-1afb23076cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391740} {:answer/id #uuid "94fc55df-9a81-5694-9adb-ccac511991c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391741}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391741} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e39085e-c8a9-5cbc-b6d2-646a14b27243" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "08d92346-a7e8-58c6-8d60-e4702d743dd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-339138" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=x{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=x{e}^{3x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y\\right) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot x{e}^{3x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1924129-59d4-51bd-b080-bb458495d76a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392577} {:answer/id #uuid "0a2ee414-1581-52ee-ade1-b3af25d669ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392578} {:answer/id #uuid "57bb0bd6-788e-5954-9630-1ba3c85bc726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No horizontal asymptotes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392579} {:answer/id #uuid "394d0a4f-4b21-5438-be5a-4733bf841070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392580} {:answer/id #uuid "395e2af3-07b7-524d-9556-f08f6f927946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=0,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392581}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392580} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a7c4c3-8dfb-5fa3-94ee-4fc77c3e36f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b7f28af0-f18c-54e2-a376-789177dbecf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-4660" :question/problem "Determine the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{1-{x}^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is ${x}^{3}.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by ${x}^{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+1}{1-{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}-1\\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ and $\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}-1\\right)} \\\\  & \\to \\frac{0+0}{0-1} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the horizontal asymptote is $y=0.$"} {:answer/id #uuid "75a85318-b190-5737-a110-a53c2d61116f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[2{\\left(3+\\frac{i}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392678} {:answer/id #uuid "4f87f8d4-091f-597f-8064-57217d4058eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[2{\\left(1+\\frac{4i}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392679} {:answer/id #uuid "e85e3aa9-96ed-523b-82db-3d9bbeb770fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[2{\\left(1+\\frac{i}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392680} {:answer/id #uuid "ee49c490-8275-50d2-afca-b5c3a6c0b061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[2{\\left(3+\\frac{i}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392681} {:answer/id #uuid "fa88e529-6995-5c09-a922-43fc40d4dc40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[2{\\left(3+\\frac{3i}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392682} {:answer/id #uuid "90ef638b-83d5-5224-a338-0b9f8dabf3c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}\\left[{\\left(2+\\frac{l}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392684} {:answer/id #uuid "caa4420a-0661-55bb-afdb-e0dbf6ba4d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}\\left[{\\left(1+\\frac{l}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392685} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8c75be-1194-556f-9e84-e70e9c10d0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}\\left[{\\left(1+\\frac{2l}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392686} {:answer/id #uuid "0be90ad5-7e03-50b9-a97a-3037376e3da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}\\left[-{\\left(2+\\frac{l}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392687} {:answer/id #uuid "7c1f7ffb-3a77-5b4f-9e74-656e7ff5708e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}\\left[{\\left(1+\\frac{2l}{n}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392688} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f685ce5-117b-5cb1-93fa-3becdf830cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The center is $(1,1)$ and the radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392900} {:answer/id #uuid "11c11b67-2a78-5959-ae9c-6b75ceabf943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392901} {:answer/id #uuid "f544673a-81cf-5a3c-8e4e-0f5345a6b56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The center is $(1,0)$ and the radius is $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392902} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb5eb2f-d647-50b3-9ec2-830264b975b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The center is $(1,1)$ and the radius is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392903} {:answer/id #uuid "68cdabe8-d960-54af-a054-681067dc1d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{10}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392904}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392900} :answer-field/id #uuid "6471e1f5-248e-565f-ace6-4ec44c15f9ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "42a574c4-fd0d-57cc-b972-6174b753f17e" :question/math-academy-id "q-64836" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(3,1)$ where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, given that $‖{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)‖=2,$ and the unit tangent vector to the curve is $\\,T(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=⟨3,1⟩,$ since the point $P(3,1)$ is at the tip of $r\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)$ and $‖{T}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\right\\rangle =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\left\\langle -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)\\right\\rangle =⟨-1,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)‖}{‖{T}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)‖}=\\frac{2}{1}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)}{‖{T}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)‖}=⟨-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+R\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)N\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =⟨3,1⟩+2⟨-1,0⟩=⟨1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840901d2-388a-56b4-b2ed-4aa835792fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle +s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393059} {:answer/id #uuid "3a999e63-69bc-5b5b-ba4a-b3d5b35bdaf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle ,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} {:answer/id #uuid "a9567360-7eeb-5790-a68a-54789a38c8f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393061} {:answer/id #uuid "0abc7499-ef02-5049-b4d5-92446ade1dde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,20⟩+t⟨0,3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393062} {:answer/id #uuid "d56ba868-cc5e-5eb8-8190-756b44636c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,0,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,7⟩+t\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle ,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} :answer-field/id #uuid "74bd7e12-82f3-5b83-88f9-1acb2c12ad74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a1e3ae2d-0bf0-5679-8209-36898e366f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70981" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $H(-3,2,7)$ and is parallel to the lines $\\mathbf{r}=⟨3,-1,20⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and $\\mathbf{r}=⟨0,3,-4⟩+t\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle .$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${\\mathbf{v}}_{\\mathbf{1}}=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{\\mathbf{2}}=\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle $, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $H(-3,2,7)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $\\mathbf{h}=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r} & =\\mathbf{h}+s{\\mathbf{v}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+t{\\mathbf{v}}_{\\mathbf{2}} \\\\ \\mathbf{r} & =⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle ,\\hspace{2em}s,t\\in (-\\mathrm{∞},\\mathrm{∞}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "840901d2-388a-56b4-b2ed-4aa835792fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle +s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393059} {:answer/id #uuid "3a999e63-69bc-5b5b-ba4a-b3d5b35bdaf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle ,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} {:answer/id #uuid "d56ba868-cc5e-5eb8-8190-756b44636c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,0,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,7⟩+t\\left\\langle 2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle ,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393063} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e308dc50-8d1a-5be8-8bbc-ac3c0f36ba24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨18t-12,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393155} {:answer/id #uuid "09d66d5c-4d57-5f45-b863-d859d6731c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨18,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393156} {:answer/id #uuid "21f4858f-79e0-56bc-b9f1-8a92538ca3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨9,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393157} {:answer/id #uuid "6e19d831-00d7-51e2-a2c5-b5965a41872f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨9,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393158} {:answer/id #uuid "de3d11e8-96e8-5e70-9677-d7323e70e0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨9t,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393159}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393156} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e1a18c0-8ad6-5833-ac15-05410c96661f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "31054e53-d905-5451-9de9-677fd754227a" :question/math-academy-id "q-7161" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨9{t}^{2}-12t,4t+17⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(9{t}^{2}-12t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t+17)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨18t-12,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(18t-12),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨18,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bb87f44-9e54-547c-bf05-ae2ff892adc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨4{t}^{3},\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393162} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4c5bec-76b9-51aa-955d-d6d64eddf07d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨6{t}^{3},\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393163} {:answer/id #uuid "783f3cce-1dea-53dc-8a90-43631ed18539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨{t}^{4},\\,3t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393164} {:answer/id #uuid "08c13741-b540-5324-ade7-9e8d1017f6ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨{t}^{3},\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393165} {:answer/id #uuid "beb86fd9-f93a-555f-a0ac-cfee71d85783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=⟨4{t}^{3},\\,6t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393166}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393162} :answer-field/id #uuid "f76bc762-0563-53c1-a43e-9693c4d41279" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "018374cc-40c9-5d0d-a1b9-641708c13290" :question/math-academy-id "q-7165" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=\\left\\langle \\frac{{t}^{5}}{5},\\,3{t}^{2}-1\\right\\rangle .\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-1)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{4},\\,6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3a993e-29b5-59cb-99e5-ded901d8bd0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393169} {:answer/id #uuid "c7002ec2-9546-5f0e-821c-ebe64ba0bd6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{19},\\frac{12}{19},-\\frac{12}{19}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393170} {:answer/id #uuid "7366fd93-b330-5afb-bffc-fc0a9d70dc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{5},\\frac{2}{5},-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393171} {:answer/id #uuid "3da3af95-6571-5bb0-ac07-5accef6e0a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393172} {:answer/id #uuid "736a78cf-613a-5d25-a09d-d0901781721f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{3}{17},\\frac{1}{17},\\frac{1}{17}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393173}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393170} :answer-field/id #uuid "81ed75df-1ce1-5ebc-81a9-b722c6382e6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4a5f805d-9915-543e-b3c6-5d61cd49da57" :question/math-academy-id "q-71662" :question/problem "Let $c=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $d=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-3)}{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{19}⟨1,3,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{19},\\frac{12}{19},-\\frac{12}{19}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "c7002ec2-9546-5f0e-821c-ebe64ba0bd6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{19},\\frac{12}{19},-\\frac{12}{19}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393170} {:answer/id #uuid "7366fd93-b330-5afb-bffc-fc0a9d70dc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{5},\\frac{2}{5},-\\frac{1}{5}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393171} {:answer/id #uuid "736a78cf-613a-5d25-a09d-d0901781721f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{3}{17},\\frac{1}{17},\\frac{1}{17}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393173} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89cf84e6-fa60-5c64-b93b-865747b163cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a(t)=1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393182} {:answer/id #uuid "ce91f5ac-68b0-5d12-b408-5805719d5633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a(t)=1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393183} {:answer/id #uuid "9153eb0d-2401-550a-8773-be6e4eb8e8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393184} {:answer/id #uuid "adae588b-ff36-562f-b371-73f948870d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a(t)=t+\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393185} {:answer/id #uuid "d5256482-56c1-5d4e-a0c1-dc867d2591d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a(t)=t-\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393182} :answer-field/id #uuid "0524bc50-6e64-5c83-9e81-cb4394c0bfc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e5248e4-d160-51d4-9bba-1d38c3c5aabb" :question/math-academy-id "q-7186" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(t-\\frac{1}{t}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-{t}^{-1}) \\\\  & =1-(-{t}^{-2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce3626c4-68fc-5111-92bb-c6a72ef04b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(e+\\frac{4ie}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{4e}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393252} {:answer/id #uuid "51976397-23e1-57d8-a039-644bf6317f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[{e}^{(-2i/n)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393253} {:answer/id #uuid "9d2df163-f8cb-55a5-aa92-94fe12f6f8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(e+\\frac{2ie}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393254} {:answer/id #uuid "680c2096-a3a6-56c7-af41-ad8e3a2a9b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[{e}^{(2i/n)}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393255} {:answer/id #uuid "7e48b7d1-54ea-5e38-b291-212dbf407565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(e+\\frac{ie}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393256}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393254} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae6ae5ee-b93f-55d8-b530-ad34a29b014a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d2f3eda7-3ae2-5c51-adcd-171934d8313e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73156" :question/problem "What is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{e}^{3e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{e}^{3e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ the lower bound is $a=e,$ and the upper bound is $b=3e.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3e-e}{n}=\\frac{2e}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{3e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[f\\left(e+i\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}\\right] \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[f\\left(e+\\frac{2ie}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}\\right] \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(e+\\frac{2ie}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3626c4-68fc-5111-92bb-c6a72ef04b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(e+\\frac{4ie}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{4e}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393252} {:answer/id #uuid "51976397-23e1-57d8-a039-644bf6317f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[{e}^{(-2i/n)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393253} {:answer/id #uuid "9d2df163-f8cb-55a5-aa92-94fe12f6f8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(e+\\frac{2ie}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2e}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393254} {:answer/id #uuid "680c2096-a3a6-56c7-af41-ad8e3a2a9b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[{e}^{(2i/n)}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393255} {:answer/id #uuid "7e48b7d1-54ea-5e38-b291-212dbf407565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(e+\\frac{ie}{n}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393256} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0da1a72-6c89-5d11-98ae-9debf71703d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\frac{1}{16}{\\left(\\frac{3l}{n}\\right)}^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393259} {:answer/id #uuid "e5dd2ac8-0379-5c8c-b3a4-1deacc410ff9" :answer/type {:db/i